+Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_MIC_DUMP=1: what a Switch 2 sysmix input stream's ring looks like (for the ocarina hum); off by default
+
+The Switch 2 Ocarina of Time plays the ocarina from a hum into the microphone. At boot it opens
+two sysmix input streams (kind 1): "InputStream-0<=1ch48kQ15<=AudioVirtualOutput0" and
+"InputStream-1<=1ch48kQ15<=TrueRawAudioIn", each 4800 frames of mono Q15 at 48 kHz in a 0xd000-byte
+ring. Eden fills neither. To feed the PS5 controller's mic into the second, where the samples go in
+the ring has to be known: only the two indices are (read at +0x44, write at +0x1004), and 0xd000
+bytes is far more than 4801 16-bit frames.
+
+With the switch, for each input stream: at open and at each attach/engage, every non-zero 32-bit
+word of the first 0x3000 bytes (at most 64), and while open both indices about once a second
+(EDEN_MIC_DUMP lines, at most 200 a session). The stream keeps CreateStream's kind for this.
+Nothing else changes, on or off.
+
